WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.670
Here is a map of equipotential
lines, marked 50,

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.500
75 and 100 volts.

3
00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:10.340
Place an electron on the
middle line, perfectly still.

4
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:11.590
Let it go.

5
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.120
Only the electric force acts on it.

6
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:15.640
Which way does it go?

7
00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:18.460
Along its own line, or across the lines?

8
00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.130
Towards higher potential, or lower?

9
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.040
And does it speed up?

10
00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:27.010
In this mission, you'll find the
potential energy of a group of charges,

11
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.050
adding every pair once.

12
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.350
Then you'll turn a map of field arrows
into a map of equipotential lines,

13
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.680
and back again.

14
00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:37.900
Your mission: predict which
way the electron moves,

15
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.550
and whether it speeds up.
